{"schema_version":"1.0","sample_id":"scale-sbrophy-dev-realms-of-iron-0144","messages":[{"role":"user","content":"Implement the `resolveNormalBattle` function in TypeScript, ensuring it adheres to the G1 code unit guidelines. The function should take three parameters: `attackerStr`, `effectiveDefender`, `rawDefenderStr`, and `rng`. It should return a `CombatResult` object with the winner, casualties, and rounds played."},{"role":"assistant","content":"function resolveNormalBattle(\n  attackerStr: number,\n  effectiveDefender: number,\n  rawDefenderStr: number,\n  rng: () => number\n): CombatResult {\n  const total = attackerStr + effectiveDefender;\n  const attackerChance = attackerStr / total;\n  const roll = rng();\n\n  const winner: 'attacker' | 'defender' = roll < attackerChance ? 'attacker' : 'defender';\n\n  // Casualties: loser takes heavier losses\n  const loserCasualtyRate = 0.3 + rng() * 0.2; // 30-50%\n  const winnerCasualtyRate = 0.1 + rng() * 0.1; // 10-20%\n\n  let attackerCasualties: number;\n  let defenderCasualties: number;\n\n  if (winner === 'attacker') {\n    attackerCasualties = Math.round(attackerStr * winnerCasualtyRate);\n    defenderCasualties = Math.round(rawDefenderStr * loserCasualtyRate);\n  } else {\n    attackerCasualties = Math.round(attackerStr * loserCasualtyRate);\n    defenderCasualties = Math.round(rawDefenderStr * winnerCasualtyRate);\n  }\n\n  return { winner, attackerCasualties, defenderCasualties, rounds: 1 };\n}\n"}],"context":{"language":"TypeScript","provided_symbols":["CombatResult","Casualties"]},"metadata":{"source_repo":"SBrophy-dev/Realms-of-Iron","source_commit":"db62fde05f0837d8e05ce5aff49360b4eb01d4b8","source_path":"src/engine/combat.ts","source_lines":"54-82","repository_family_id":"github-family:SBrophy-dev/Realms-of-Iron","license":"MIT","category":"tactics","granularity":"G1","symbol":"resolveNormalBattle","target_sha256":"e6862bf40fab46d30272d367ca0d49add249edeac4b8a5a3d4ad5eb6d22ffc8d","generation":{"model":